./analysis/cross_agent_screening_agreement_current_3ds_2gpt/unstable_reasoning_cases.csv:37:1236,Language may be all omics needs: Harmonizing multimodal data for omics understanding with CellHermes,stable_include,INCLUDE|INCLUDE|INCLUDE|INCLUDE|EXCLUDE,INCLUDE,,,,,,,"CellHermes is presented as a primary model that uses natural language question-answer pairs to integrate and process omics data, clearly satisfying both text component and text-bio bridge criteria. | CellHermes fine-tunes an existing LLM via LORA on question-answer pairs for multimodal omics tasks, demonstrating generative capabilities and foundation-model-like broad applicability.",INCLUDE,,,,,,,"CellHermes is a primary model that integrates omics data via natural language question-answer pairs and text-based reasoning, clearly satisfying all inclusion criteria. | CellHermes fine-tunes a pretrained LLM with LORA on omics question-answer pairs, enabling generative prediction and explanation across multiple tasks, demonstrating foundation-model characteristics.",INCLUDE,,,,,,,"CellHermes is a primary candidate model that integrates omics data via natural language question-answer pairs, with clear text-bio bridge central to its functions as encoder, predictor, and explainer. | CellHermes fine-tunes an existing LLM via LORA to generate text answers for omics tasks, showing generative capability and foundation-model-like broad applicability across multiple biological tasks.",INCLUDE,,,clear_include,reformulating datasets into natural language question‑answer pairs,integrates multimodal omics data through natural language as a unifying medium,allows a single model to perform multi‑task prediction by generating answers and explanations,"The abstract presents CellHermes as a new multimodal language model that leverages pretrained LLMs, uses natural‑language QA pairs, and generates answers/explanations, satisfying all inclusion criteria.",EXCLUDE,EC3_not_generative,,,,,,"The abstract presents CellHermes as a new model that reformulates omics data into natural‑language question‑answer pairs and uses a pretrained LLM, providing clear evidence of a substantive text‑bio bridge. | The abstract presents CellHermes as an encoder, predictor, and explainer without mentioning a decoder or any generative mechanism, so it is not a generative model; however, it leverages pretrained LLMs and claims broad applicability, providing foundation‑model evidence.",wrapper_boundary;text_component_boundary;generative_boundary
