nguage summaries, showing a generative decoder mechanism, and it leverages gene‑level embeddings from single‑cell foundation models and pretrained LLMs, indicating foundation‑model characteristics.", "pilot_roundA_scope_gate": "PASS", "pilot_roundA_architecture_gate": "PASS", "pilot_needs_adjudication": false}
./analysis/screening_run_artifacts_after_prompt_update_20260511/full_runs/gpt_oss_120b_review_pipeline_all4027_current_watchdog_20260511T1116Z/job_11550/guideline_pilot_raw_completed.jsonl:1878:{"cluster_id": 1988, "title": "Sequence-to-Temperature: RAG-Enhanced and XAI-Supported OGT Estimation from Archaea tRNA Sequences Using Transformer-Based Embeddings", "title_normalized": "sequencetotemperature ragenhanced and xaisupported ogt estimation from archaea trna sequences using transformerbased embeddings", "doi": "10.1109/BIBE66822.2025.00068", "preprint_doi": NaN, "pmid": NaN, "arxiv_id": NaN, "abstract": "The growth conditions of an organism play a critical role in its biological characterization. However, information regarding these conditions is often unavailable. Predicting the optimal growth temperature based on the physical properties of the genome allows for estimation without the need to culture newly discovered species. In this context, developing methods that infer an organism's ideal growth temperature from genomic sequence data represents an important approach for improving efficiency in both time and resource management. In this study, we propose a novel methodology that leverages the structural parallels between tRNA sequences and natural language through transformerbased models. The approach comprises three main components: (i) generating embedding vectors from tRNA sequences using transformer-based encoders, (ii) storing and retrieving these embeddings within a vector-based database via a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) architecture, and (iii) performing a regression task using a large language model (LLM) based on the retrieved sequences, enhanced with explainable AI techniques to provide interpretable predictions. This framework introduces an alternative and interpretable solution for optimal growth temperature (OGT) estimation, highlighting the utility of RAG architectures in genomic applications.", "authors": "Ahmet Telçeken; Eyup Cinar", "year": 2025.0, "venue": "International Conferences on Biological Information and Biomedical Engineering", "date": "2025-11-06", "url": NaN, "sources": "['semantic_scholar']", "n_sources": 1, "all_dois": "['10.1109/BIBE66822.2025.00068']", "duplicate_count": 1, "abstract_source": NaN, "abstract_enriched_from": NaN, "abstract_old_len": NaN, "update_batch": NaN, "_pilot_row_id": 1856, "round-A_scope_reviewer_output": {"paper_type": "primary_model_paper", "bio_modality_present": "yes", "text_component_present": "no", "text_bio_bridge_present": "no", "primary_exclusion_code": "none", "uncertainty_reason": "none", "evidence_for_text_component": "none", "evidence_for_text_bio_bridge": "none", "evidence_for_generative_model": "not_assessed", "boundary_case": "none", "decision_rationale": "The abstract proposes a novel transformer‑based embedding and RAG pipeline to predict optimal growth temperature from tRNA sequences, without describing natural‑language text inputs, prompts, or generation, thus lacking a substantive text component or text‑bio bridge."}, "round-A_scope_reviewer_paper_type": "primary_model_paper", "round-A_scope_reviewer_bio_modality_present": "yes", "round-A_scope_reviewer_text_component_present": "no", "round-A_scope_reviewer_text_bio_bridge_present": "no", "round-A_scope_reviewer_primary_exclusion_code": "none", "round-A_scope_reviewer_uncertainty_reason": "none", "round-A_scope_reviewer_evidence_for_text_component": "none", "round-A_scope_reviewer_evidence_for_text_bio_bridge": "none", "round-A_scope_reviewer_evidence_for_generative_model": "not_assessed", "round-A_scope_reviewer_boundary_case": "none", "round-A_scope_reviewer_decision_rationale": "The abstract proposes a novel transformer‑based embedding and RAG pipeline to predict optimal growth temperature from tRNA sequences, without describing natural‑language text inputs, prompts, or generation, thus lacking a substantive text component or text‑bio bridge.", "round-A_architecture_reviewer_output":