erform multi‑task prediction by generating answers and explanations,clear_include,"The abstract presents CellHermes as a new multimodal language model that leverages pretrained LLMs, uses natural‑language QA pairs, and generates answers/explanations, satisfying all inclusion criteria.","The abstract presents CellHermes as a new multimodal model that encodes omics data via natural‑language question‑answer reformulation, indicating a substantive text component and a central text‑bio bridge.","The abstract describes a model fine‑tuned on LLMs for question‑answer prediction but does not explicitly mention a decoder, autoregressive, or other generative mechanism, so generative status is unclear; however, it clearly leverages pretrained LLMs, indicating foundation‑model characteristics.","The abstract presents CellHermes as a new multimodal language model that leverages pretrained LLMs, uses natural‑language QA pairs, and generates answers/explanations, satisfying all inclusion criteria.",Language may be all omics needs: Harmonizing multimodal data for omics understanding with CellHermes,"Decoding cellular systems requires integrating diverse omics data, yet most models are trained from scratch on a single modality, restricting generalization. Here we present CellHermes, a biological language model that leverages pretrained large language models (LLMs) to integrate multimodal forms of omics data, such as transcriptomic profile and PPI network, through natural language for better omics understanding. By reformulating these datasets into question-answer pairs, CellHermes emulates multiple self-supervised learning paradigms within a single, universal, language-based framework with LORA fine-tuning on existing natural language-LLM, achieving comparable or even better performance compared to current single-cell foundation models. Within this framework, CellHermes functions as an encoder, a predictor and an explainer for supporting a range of downstream tasks. For encoder, CellHermes encodes biological entities with embeddings that enable accurate network discovery and cross-dataset generalization; For predictor, CellHermes unifies heterogeneous downstream tasks by translating them into natural language question-answers pairs, allowing a single model to perform multi-task prediction by instruction fine-tuning; For explainer, CellHermes explains molecular mechanisms by combining attention analysis with text-based reasoning, leveraging the interpretability and reasoning capabilities of LLMs. We evaluated the ability of CellHermes as an  encoder on representing genes and cells using 5 gene-level downstream tasks and 5 diverse single-cell datasets across different tissues compared with other single cell foundation models. We also evaluated CellHermes as a  predictor on BioUniBench, a new benchmark of 10 tasks across 7 databases for LLMs, including perturbation response, cell fitness estimation, gene-disease association, and cell type identification. All benchmarks suggest CellHermes can unify multiple biological tasks within one model without compromising performance. By applying CellHermes as an  explainer for a melanoma patients dataset, it can uncover potential key genes on tumor-reactive T cells. Together, CellHermes establishes natural language as a unifying medium for omics, offering a foundation that, in the future, potentially enables a more integrated and interpretable research loop of biological representation, prediction, and interpretability.",stable_include,EXCLUDE,EC3_not_generative,,primary_model_paper,yes,yes,no,yes,,,,,"The abstract presents CellHermes as a new model that reformulates omics data into natural‑language question‑answer pairs and uses a pretrained LLM, providing clear evidence of a substantive text‑bio bridge. | The abstract presents CellHermes as an encoder, predictor, and explainer without mentioning a decoder or any generative mechanism, so it is not a generative model; however, it leverages pretrained LLMs and claims broad applicability, providing foundation‑model evidence.","The abstract presents CellHermes as a new model that reformulates omics data into natural‑language question‑answer pairs and uses a pretrained LLM, providing clear evidence of a substantive text‑bio bridge.","The abstract presents CellHermes as an encoder, predictor, and explainer without mentioning a decoder or any generative mechanism, so it is not a generative model; however, it leverages pretrained LLMs and claims broad applicability, providing foundation‑model evidence.",
./analysis/cross_agent_screening_agreement/cross_model_decisions.csv:564:882,Multimodal learning enables chat-based exploration of single-cell data,"CellWhisperer uses multimodal learning of transcriptomes and text to answer questions about single-cell RNA-sequencing data. Single-cell sequencing characterizes biological samples at unprecedented scale and detail, but data interpretation remains challenging. Here, we present CellWhisperer, an artificial intelligence (AI) model and software tool for chat-based interrogation of gene expression. We establish a multimodal embedding of transcriptomes and their textual annotations, using contrastive learning on 1 million RNA sequencing profiles with AI-curated descriptions. This embedding informs a large language model that answers user-provided questions about cells and genes in natural-language chats. We benchmark CellWhisperer’s performance for zero-shot prediction of cell types and other biological annotations and demonstrate its use for biological discovery in a meta-analysis of human embryonic development. We integrate a CellWhisperer chat box with the CELLxGENE browser, allowing users to interactively explore gene expression through a combined graphical and chat interface. In summary, CellWhisperer leverages large community-scale data repositories to connect transcriptomes and text, thereby enabling interactive exploration of single-cell RNA-sequencing data with natural-language chats.",stable_include,Multimodal learning enables chat-based exploration of single-cell data,"CellWhisperer uses multimodal learning of transcriptomes and text to answer questions about single-cell RNA-sequencing data. Single-cell sequencing characterizes biological samples at unprecedented scale and detail, but data interpretation remains challenging. Here, we present CellWhisperer, an artificial intelligence (AI) model and software tool for chat-based interrogation of gene expression. We establish a multimodal embedding of transcriptomes and their textual annotations, using contrastive learning on 1 million RNA sequencing profiles with AI-curated descriptions. This embedding informs a large language model that answers user-provided questions about cells and genes in natural-language chats. We benchmark CellWhisperer’s performance for zero-shot prediction of cell types and other biological annotations and demonstrate its use for biological discovery in a meta-analysis of human embryonic development. We integrate a CellWhisperer chat box with the CELLxGENE browser, allowing users to interactively explore gene expression through a combined graphical and chat interface. In summary, CellWhisperer leverages large community-scale data repositories to connect transcriptomes and text, thereby enabling interactive exploration of single-cell RNA-sequencing data with natural-language chats.",stable_include,INCLUDE,,,primary_model_paper,yes,yes,yes,yes,"textual annotations, natural-language chats, user-provided questions",multimodal embedding of transcriptomes and their textual annotations using contrastive learning,large language model that answers user-provided questions about cells and genes in natural-language chats,clear_include,"CellWhisperer is presented as a new multimodal model that learns joint embeddings of transcriptomes and text, then uses an LLM for chat-based generation, which is a primary generative model paper, not a wrapper.","The abstract presents CellWhisperer as a new multimodal model that links transcriptomes and natural language for chat-based interrogation, clearly satisfying all criteria.","CellWhisperer uses a pretrained LLM for chat-based interrogation; the main contribution is a multimodal embedding, making it an application wrapper rather than a primary generative model.","CellWhisperer is presented as a new multimodal model that learns joint embeddings of transcriptomes and text, then uses an LLM for chat-based generation, which is a primary generative model paper, not a wrapper.",Multimodal learning enables chat-based exploration of single-cell data,"CellWhisperer uses multimodal learning of transcriptomes and text to answer questions about single-cell RNA-sequencing data. Single-cell sequencing characterizes biological samples at unprecedented scale and detail, but data interpretation remains challenging. Here, we present CellWhisperer, an artificial intelligence (AI) model and software tool for chat-based interrogation of gene expression. We establish a multimodal embedding of transcriptomes and their textual annotations, using contrastive learning on 1 million RNA sequencing profiles with AI-curated descriptions. This embedding informs a large language model that answers user-provided questions about cells and genes in natural-language chats. We benchmark CellWhisperer’s performance for zero-shot prediction of cell types and other biological annotations and demonstrate its use for biological discovery in a meta-analysis of human embryonic development. We integrate a CellWhisperer chat box with the CELLxGENE browser, allowing users to interactively explore gene expression through a combined graphical and chat interface. In summary, CellWhisperer leverages large community-scale data repositories to connect transcriptomes and text, thereby enabling interactive exploration of single-cell RNA-sequencing data with natural-language chats.",stable_include,INCLUDE,,,primary_model_paper,yes,yes,yes,unclear,"natural-language chats, textual annotations, user-provided questions","multimodal embedding of transcriptomes and text, connect transcriptomes and text","large language model that answers user-provided questions, chat-based interrogation",clear_include,"Abstract describes CellWhisperer as a new multimodal AI model that learns joint embeddings of transcriptomes and text to enable chat-based generation of answers, not a wrapper; all decisive criteria are clearly supported.","CellWhisperer is a new AI model that uses multimodal learning to align transcriptomes with natural-language text for chat-based question answering, clearly meeting all criteria for a primary text-bio model.","CellWhisperer uses a pre-existing large language model for chat-based responses; the core contribution is a multimodal embedding and integration, not a new generative foundation model.","Abstract describes CellWhisperer as a new multimodal AI model that learns joint embeddings of transcriptomes and text to enable chat-based generation of answers, not a wrapper; all decisive criteria are clearly supported.",Multimodal learning enables chat-based exploration of single-cell data,"CellWhisperer uses multimodal learning of transcriptomes and text to answer questions about single-cell RNA-sequencing data. Single-cell sequencing characterizes biological samples at unprecedented scale and detail, but data interpretation remains challenging. Here, we present CellWhisperer, an artificial intelligence (AI) model and software tool for chat-based interrogation of gene expression. We establish a multimodal embedding of transcriptomes and their textual annotations, using contrastive learning on 1 million RNA sequencing profiles with AI-curated descriptions. This embedding informs a large language model that answers user-provided questions about cells and genes in natural-language chats. We benchmark CellWhisperer’s performance for zero-shot prediction of cell types and other biological annotations and demonstrate its use for biological discovery in a meta-analysis of human embryonic development. We integrate a CellWhisperer chat box with the CELLxGENE browser, allowing users to interactively explore gene expression through a combined graphical and chat interface. In summary, CellWhisperer leverages large community-scale data repositories to connect transcriptomes and text, thereby enabling interactive exploration of single-cell RNA-sequencing data with natural-language chats.",stable_include,INCLUDE,,,primary_model_paper,yes,yes,yes,yes,,,,,"The abstract presents CellWhisperer as a new AI model that jointly learns transcriptome data and textual annotations, and uses a large language model to answer natural‑language questions, indicating a primary model with both biological modality and substantive text‑bio bridge. | The abstract presents CellWhisperer, a multimodal model trained on 1 M RNA profiles that leverages a large language model to generate natural‑language answers, indicating a generative architecture with foundation‑model‑like pretraining.","The abstract presents CellWhisperer as a new AI model that jointly learns transcriptome data and textual annotations, and uses a large language model to answer natural‑language questions, indicating a primary model with both biological modality and substantive text‑bio bridge.","The abstract presents CellWhisperer, a multimodal model trained on 1 M RNA profiles that leverages a large language model to generate natural‑language answers, indicating a generative architecture with foundation‑model‑like pretraining.",,Multimodal learning enables chat-based exploration of single-cell data,"CellWhisperer uses multimodal learning of transcriptomes and text to answer questions about single-cell RNA-sequencing data. Single-cell sequencing characterizes biological samples at unprecedented scale and detail, but data interpretation remains challenging. Here, we present CellWhisperer, an artificial intelligence (AI) model and software tool for chat-based interrogation of gene expression. We establish a multimodal embedding of transcriptomes and their textual annotations, using contrastive learning on 1 million RNA sequencing profiles with AI-curated descriptions. This embedding informs a large language model that answers user-provided questions about cells and genes in natural-language chats. We benchmark CellWhisperer’s performance for zero-shot prediction of cell types and other biological annotations and demonstrate its use for biological discovery in a meta-analysis of human embryonic development. We integrate a CellWhisperer chat box with the CELLxGENE browser, allowing users to interactively explore gene expression through a combined graphical and chat interface. In summary, CellWhisperer leverages large community-scale data repositories to connect transcriptomes and text, thereby enabling interactive exploration of single-cell RNA-sequencing data with natural-language chats.",stable_include,INCLUDE,,,primary_model_paper,yes,yes,yes,yes,,,,,"The abstract presents CellWhisperer as a new multimodal AI model that jointly embeds single‑cell RNA‑seq data and text, and uses a large language model for chat‑based interrogation, satisfying the criteria for a primary model with both biological modality and a substantive text‑bio bridge. | The abstract introduces CellWhisperer, a multimodal model that feeds a large language model to generate natural-language answers, showing a generative architecture and broad pretraining on 1 M RNA profiles.","The abstract presents CellWhisperer as a new multimodal AI model that jointly embeds single‑cell RNA‑seq data and text, and uses a large language model for chat‑based interrogation, satisfying the criteria for a primary model with both biological modality and a substantive text‑bio bridge.","The abstract introduces CellWhisperer, a multimodal model that feeds a large language model to generate natural-language answers, showing a generative architecture and broad pretraining on 1 M RNA profiles.",
./analysis/cross_agent_screening_agreement/unstable_reasoning_cases.csv:34:1236,Language may be all omics needs: Harmonizing multimodal data for omics understanding with CellHermes,stable_include,INCLUDE|INCLUDE|INCLUDE|EXCLUDE,INCLUDE,,,,,,,"CellHermes is presented as a primary model that uses natural language question-answer pairs to integrate and process omics data, clearly satisfying both text component and text-bio bridge criteria. | CellHermes fine-tunes an existing LLM via LORA on question-answer pairs for multimodal omics tasks, demonstrating generative capabilities and foundation-model-like broad applicability.",INCLUDE,,,,,,,"CellHermes is a primary model that integrates omics data via natural language question-answer pairs and text-based reasoning, clearly satisfying all inclusion criteria. | CellHermes fine-tunes a pretrained LLM with LORA on omics question-answer pairs, enabling generative prediction and explanation across multiple tasks, demonstrating foundation-model characteristics.",INCLUDE,,,clear_include,reformulating datasets into natural language question‑answer pairs,integrates multimodal omics data through natural language as a unifying medium,allows a single model to perform multi‑task prediction by generating answers and explanations,"The abstract presents CellHermes as a new multimodal language model that leverages pretrained LLMs, uses natural‑language QA pairs, and generates answers/explanations, satisfying all inclusion criteria.",EXCLUDE,EC3_not_generative,,,,,,"The abstract presents CellHermes as a new model that reformulates omics data into natural‑language question‑answer pairs and uses a pretrained LLM, providing clear evidence of a substantive text‑bio bridge. | The abstract presents CellHermes as an encoder, predictor, and explainer without mentioning a decoder or any generative mechanism, so it is not a generative model; however, it leverages pretrained LLMs and claims broad applicability, providing foundation‑model evidence.",wr