e":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract states this is a comprehensive review of contrastive learning in medical AI. It spans biomedical modalities and NLP, but remains a review rather than a candidate model paper.","evidence_snippet":"\"This paper presents a comprehensive review\" and \"medical imaging, electronic health records, physiological signal analysis, and genomics\""},{"record_id":"rec_001909","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a primary deep-learning model for multi-omics survival prediction. The modality is biological data only, with no text/language component described.","evidence_snippet":"\"integrate multi-omics data (e.g., gene expression, DNA methylation, miRNA expression, and copy number variations)\""},{"record_id":"rec_001910","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_substantive_text_bio_bridge","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The work uses genomic large language models and inverse folding to design RNA sequences. However, the abstract supports bio-sequence modeling rather than a substantive text-bio bridge.","evidence_snippet":"\"integrates genomic large language models (LLMs) with inverse folding models\" and \"generate RNA sequences\""},{"record_id":"rec_001911","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a primary multimodal topic model for single-cell multiomics. The abstract concerns transcriptomic, epigenomic, and proteomic data, with no text/language component.","evidence_snippet":"\"single-cell multiomics assays simultaneously measure transcriptomic, epigenomic, and proteomic modalities\""},{"record_id":"rec_001912","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a primary bioimage synthesis method for multiplex immunofluorescence and H&E data. The transformer and masked language modeling are used over visual tokens, not a substantive text component.","evidence_snippet":"\"channel-wise bioimage synthesis\" and \"a bidirectional transformer infers missing markers through masked language modeling\""}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0113.stderr.log:933:./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0293.response.txt:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_002337","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract says this is a comprehensive overview and explicitly states, 'This review synthesizes current research.' It discusses NLP and omics in drug discovery, but as a review rather than a primary model paper.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review synthesizes current research\" and \"including natural language processing techniques\""},{"record_id":"rec_002338","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The work integrates 'language- and transformer-based models' with MS-genome datasets to identify microbial producers. This is a substantive text-bio model bridge rather than a review or wrapper.","evidence_snippet":"\"integrating language- and transformer-based models to cross-validate mass spectrometry (MS)-genome datasets\""},{"record_id":"rec_002339","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract presents a new genomic language-model framework and trains PhyloGPN on whole-genome alignments. The language-modeling component is central to the biological task.","evidence_snippet":"\"introduce a novel framework for training gLMs\" and \"train PhyloGPN\""},{"record_id":"rec_002340","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a radiogenomics model that predicts gene expression from MRI images. The abstract contains no substantive text or language component.","evidence_snippet":"\"predicts the expression contents of genetic factors ... using MRI images\""},{"record_id":"rec_002341","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"GenoCGC is a CNN/Graphormer model for genomic sequence classification. The mention of genomic large language models is only for comparison, not part of the candidate model.","evidence_snippet":"\"hybrid model combining Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) and a Graph-based Transformer\" and \"compared GenoCGC ... with genomic large language models\""},{"record_id":"rec_002342","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"EP2vec uses embeddings learned using an unsupervised NLP method and then trains a classifier for EPI prediction. That is a downstream wrapper around NLP-derived features.","evidence_snippet":"\"sequence embedding features ... learned ... using an unsupervised deep learning method in natural language processing\""},{"record_id":"rec_002343","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract proposes a modified VAE for integrating omics modalities and predicting drug response. It is purely biological/modal data, with no text component.","evidence_snippet":"\"apply similar approaches to correct large omics measurements across various cancer datasets\""},{"record_id":"rec_002344","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"no","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a conference 'Preface' describing proceedings and tracks, not an original model paper. It does not present a biological modality or text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"\"Preface\" and \"the conference ... proceedings ... tracks\""}]}
