./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0383.stderr.log:1761:./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0141.stdout.log:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_001121","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract centers on creating the MSK-CHORD dataset and infrastructure, not introducing a new candidate foundation model. NLP is used to annotate free-text clinical reports for a resource buildout.","evidence_snippet":"\"Systematic generation of a clinicogenomic harmonized oncologic real-world dataset (MSK-CHORD)\"; \"NLP could automatically annotate\"; \"create a Clinicogenomic, Harmonized Oncologic Real-world Dataset\""},{"record_id":"rec_001122","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a self-supervised model on neuronal population recordings with transcriptomic labels used downstream. The abstract does not describe a substantive text/language component in the candidate model.","evidence_snippet":"\"self-supervised learning based method\"; \"population recordings\"; \"molecular (transcriptomic) labels for downstream supervised tasks\""},{"record_id":"rec_001123","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract presents a gene-based language model and a Transformer trained to produce genome representations. It explicitly frames gene content as language and uses that bridge for model learning.","evidence_snippet":"\"gene-based language model\"; \"Transformer model\"; 