w of contrastive learning in medical AI, so it is not a primary generative model report. The abstract discusses methods and future directions rather than a candidate foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"This paper presents a comprehensive review of contrastive learning in medical AI\""},{"record_id":"rec_001909","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC4_no_foundation_model_evidence","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly describes autoencoder models for multi-omics integration, which is a generative/reconstructive architecture. However, it does not show broad pretraining or other foundation-model-like characteristics.","evidence_snippet":"\"we develop a concatenation autoencoder (ConcatAE)\" and \"a cross-modality autoencoder (CrossAE)\""},{"record_id":"rec_001910","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract presents a zero-shot RNA design strategy that uses genomic large language models and inverse folding models to generate sequences. It explicitly reports benchmarking multiple genomic foundation models and zero-shot transfer.","evidence_snippet":"\"integrates genomic large language models (LLMs) with inverse folding models\"; \"Benchmarking 9 state-of-the-art genomic foundation models\""},{"record_id":"rec_001911","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC4_no_foundation_model_evidence","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes EpiConfig as a multimodal topic model, which is a generative probabilistic model. It does not provide evidence of broad pretraining, transferability, or foundation-model-like scope.","evidence_snippet":"\"EpiConfig is a multimodal topic model\"; \"