./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0141.stdout.log:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_001121","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a dataset-generation and annotation pipeline using NLP transformers and rule-based models, not a new generative model. The abstract describes automated curation of a harmonized dataset and downstream analysis.","evidence_snippet":"\"train and validate several Transformer and rule based-based NLP models\"; \"create a Clinicogenomic, Harmonized Oncologic Real-world Dataset (MSK-CHORD)\""},{"record_id":"rec_001122","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The method is a self-supervised representation learner for neuronal activity, with no explicit generative architecture. The abstract focuses on embeddings and downstream prediction rather than generation or broad pretraining.","evidence_snippet":"\"self-supervised learning based method to assign time-invariant representations\"; \"predicting the transcriptomic subclass identity\""},{"record_id":"rec_001123","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract presents a Transformer-based genome representation learner, but not a clearly generative model. It does give evidence of broad self-supervised pretraining and transferable representations across species and tasks.","evidence_snippet":"\"trained a Transformer model to backpropagate information into dense genome vector representations\"; \"state-of-the-art genomic supervised prediction accuracy in 11 out of 12 antibiotic resistance phenotypes\""},{"record_id":"rec_001124","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"MICE is described as a multimodal foundation model, but the abstract frames it as a prognosis prediction system, not a generative architecture. It does provide foundation-model-like evidence through broad multimodal training and generalizability.","evidence_snippet":"\"a multimodal foundation model\"; \"integrates pathology images, clinical reports, and genomics data\"; \"enhanced MICE's generalizability\""},{"record_id":"rec_001125","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC4_no_foundation_model_evidence","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"The model includes a VAE and pretraining, but the abstract describes survival-risk prediction and encoding rather than an explicit generative workflow. It does not show broad pretraining or foundation-model-like transfer across diverse tasks or domains.","evidence_snippet":"\"integrating a Transformer encoder with VAE\"; \"predict patients’ survival risk using cancer multi-omics data\""},{"record_id":"rec_001126","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a biological language model built by leveraging pretrained LLMs with LoRA fine-tuning, so the generative language-model basis is explicit. Because it is centered on adapting existing LLMs for omics tasks, it reads as an application wrapper rather than a new foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"leverages pretrained large language models (LLMs)\"; \"question-answer pairs\"; \"LoRA fine-tuning\""},{"record_id":"rec_001127","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The framework is a predictive/explainable AI system that generates biomarker hypotheses and drug-combination suggestions, but the abstract does not describe a generative model architecture. It emphasizes learned embeddings and response prediction from drug-response data.","evidence_snippet":"\"learns molecular mechanisms of drug sensitivity and resistance\"; \"generate biomarker strategies\"; \"propose rational drug-drug combinations\""},{"record_id":"rec_001128","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Exceiver is presented as a self-supervised representation model for gene expression, not as a clearly generative architecture. The abstract does support foundation-model-like evidence through training across diverse cell types and transfer learning.","evidence_snippet":"\"trained across a diversity of cell types using a self-supervised task\"; \"pretraining supports transfer learning\""}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0430.stderr.log:1497:./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0141.stdout.log:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_001121","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract centers on creating the MSK-CHORD dataset and infrastructure, not introducing a new candidate foundation model. NLP is used to annotate free-text clinical reports for a resource buildout.","evidence_snippet":"\"Systematic generation of a clinicogenomic harmonized oncologic real-world dataset (MSK-CHORD)\"; \"NLP could automatically annotate\"; \"create a Clinicogenomic, Harmonized Oncologic Real-world Dataset\""},{"record_id":"rec_001122","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a self-supervised model on neuronal population recordings with transcriptomic labels used downstream. The abstract does not describe a substantive text/language component in the candidate model.","evidence_snippet":"\"self-supervised learning based method\"; \"population recordings\"; \"molecular (transcriptomic) labels for downstream supervised tasks\""},{"record_id":"rec_001123","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract presents a gene-based language model and a Transformer trained to produce genome representations. It explicitly frames gene content as language and uses that bridge for model learning.","evidence_snippet":"\"gene-based language model\"; \"Transformer model\"; 