g CT, MRI, histology, genomic, and clinical records\""},{"record_id":"rec_001908","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract states this is a comprehensive review of contrastive learning in medical AI. It spans biomedical modalities and NLP, but remains a review rather than a candidate model paper.","evidence_snippet":"\"This paper presents a comprehensive review\" and \"medical imaging, electronic health records, physiological signal analysis, and genomics\""},{"record_id":"rec_001909","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a primary deep-learning model for multi-omics survival prediction. The modality is biological data only, with no text/language component described.","evidence_snippet":"\"integrate multi-omics data (e.g., gene expression, DNA methylation, miRNA expression, and copy number variations)\""},{"record_id":"rec_001910","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_substantive_text_bio_bridge","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The work uses genomic large language models and inverse folding to design RNA sequences. However, the abstract supports bio-sequence modeling rather than a substantive text-bio bridge.","evidence_snippet":"\"integrates genomic large language models (LLMs) with inverse folding models\" and \"generate RNA sequences\""},{"record_id":"rec_001911","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_rea